hadiths[72]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1586",": 1568 This hadith is narrated along with another document."
"1587",": 1569 The same tradition is also transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but it also contains these words: In the low part of the rocky land of Banubayzah where plants grow and which is called \Naqee Al-Khuzmat\"" the rest of the tradition is the same as the previous tradition."""""
"1588",": 1570 Amro bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather: Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the voice (of the muezzin)."
"1589",": 1571 Amro bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father and his grandfather: \Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the voice of wisdom.\"""""""
"1590",": 1572 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Friday is obligatory on the person who listens to the call to prayer on Friday."
"1591",": 1573 The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, the word \Tazeen\"" is used here."""""
"1592",": 1574 Sayyidah Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Friday is obligatory for those who live in every settlement, even if only four people remain in that settlement."
"1593",": 1575 Sayyidah Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It is obligatory to read the Friday prayer for those living in a Haras settlement, in which the Imam is present, even though there are only four people present in this settlement."
"1594",": 1576 Sayyida Umm Abdullah Dusiyah (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: It is obligatory for the residents of every town to read Friday, even if only three people remain there and the fourth is their imam."
"1595",": 1577 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday, he should add another rak'ah to it."
"1596",": 1578 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday should perform another rak'ah along with it."
"1597",": 1579 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should offer the second rak'ah along with it, and if he finds the people in a gathering during the Friday prayer, then he should offer four rak'ahs."
"1598",": 1580: Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Whoever finds one rak'ah of Friday, let him perform another rak'ah along with it."
"1599",": 1581 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): Whoever finds one rak'ah of the Friday prayer, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it."
"1600",": 1582 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and if he finds people in a state of burning, then he should perform four rak'ahs."
"1601",": 1583 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever prays one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and whoever misses two rak'ahs, then he should perform four rak'ahs (Zhuhr)."
"1602",": 1584 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a person observes two rak'ahs of Friday, he has observed the Friday prayer. The words are equivalent."
"1603",": 1585 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: He who prays the second rak'ah on Friday should perform the second rak'ah along with it, and whoever does not perform the rak'ah of the second rak'ah should perform the four rak'ahs of Zuhr."
"1604",": 1586 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet (SAW) saying: When you perform the second rak'at of Friday, perform another rak'at along with it, and if the second rak'at is also missed, then perform four rak'ats of Zuhr."
"1605",": 1587 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) said this: Whoever finds the Imam in a state of assembly, 'He did not return the salam', then he performed this prayer."
"1606","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever performs one rak’at of the Friday prayer or any other prayer, then he adds a second rak’at to it, then his prayer will be complete. is:"
"1607",": 1589 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Whoever observes one rak'ah of Friday, he should add another rak'ah to it."
"1608",": 1590 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: Whoever observes one rak'ah in Friday (Friday prayer) has observed this prayer and adds another rak'ah to it."
"1609",": 1591 Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (SAW) said this: When one of you observes one rak'ah of Friday, he should perform another rak'ah along with it."
"1610",": 1592 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) came, the Prophet (PBUH) was delivering the sermon on Friday. If you are giving a sermon, then that person should perform two rak'ahs and perform them briefly."
"1611",": 1593 Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) came. The Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to the people at that time. He sat down. The Prophet (PBUH) said: When a person comes on Friday and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time, that person should perform two short rak'ahs and then sit down."
"1612",": 1594 Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (RA) narrated this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: When someone from among you comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon, he should perform two short rak'ahs and perform them quickly."
"1613",": 1595 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this during the sermon: When a person from among you comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon at that time, the narrator has this doubt."
"1614",": 1596 Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW): When a person comes and the Imam is delivering the sermon at that time, then that person performs two rak'ahs. So he replied: Yes!"
"1615",": 1597 Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this while giving a sermon: When a person comes and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time, and that person should perform two rak'ahs."
"1616",": 1598 Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this while giving a sermon: \When a person comes and the Imam is giving a sermon at that time"","" that person should perform two rak'ahs.\"""""""
"1617",": 1599 Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was giving a sermon on Friday, while a person came in and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray two rak'ahs."
"1618",": 1600 Narrated Anas: A man from the tribe of Qays entered (the mosque). The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon at that time. It is correct: this Mu'tamarnami has been transmitted as a messenger tradition with reference to the narrator's father, but Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal has narrated it in the same way."
"1619",": 1601 Mu'tamar narrates this statement of his father: A person came (inside the mosque) while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was giving a sermon. Have you prayed? He said: No! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So you should pray. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept waiting for him until he prayed."
"1620",": 1602 Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radi Allahu Anhu narrates: On Friday, Sayyidna Salik Ghatfani (Radi Allahu Anhu) entered (inside the mosque) and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Pray two rak'ats and do not do it again."
"1621",": 1603 Muhammad bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray two rak'ahs, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped the sermon until he had finished two rak'ahs, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued his sermon."
"1622",": 1604 Muhammad bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed him to pray this prayer, he stopped his sermon until he had finished praying."
"1623",": 1605 Abdullah bin Saidan Salmi narrates: I performed the Friday prayer following the example of Sayyidna Abu Bakr, his prayer and his sermon used to be before noon."
"1624",": 1606 Iyas bin Salamah narrates this statement of his father: We used to perform the Friday prayer with our father following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then when we came back we did not find any shade under which we should come."
"1625",": 1607 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: We used to do qilaulah after Friday and eat food."
"1626",": 1608 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: We used to do qilaula after Friday and eat food."
"1627",": 1609 The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad (RA)."
"1628",": 1610 Sahl bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to perform the Friday prayer following the example of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then there would be Qailula after that."
"1629",": 1611 Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) narrates: We used to leave early to perform the Friday prayer following the example of the Prophet (PBUH), then when we came back, we would eat lunch and do Qilaula."
"1630",": 1612 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to deliver two sermons."
"1631",": 1613 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: There are three things that are obligatory on me and for you they are nafl: performing the sacrifice, performing the Witr prayer, and performing two rak'ahs of the Fajr Sunnah."
"1632",": 1614 Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been ordered to perform Witr prayer and sacrifice and I have not been obliged to do so."
"1633",": 1615 Saeed bin Yasarbayan says: I was traveling on the way to Makkah with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. Sayyid narrates: When I had this apprehension that the dawn was about to dawn, I got off the horse and offered the Witr prayer. Then I came to meet Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, asked me: Where did you stay? I said: I was afraid of being honest in the morning, so I got down from the horse and went to pray. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar asked: Is it not enough for you to follow the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace?"
"1634",": 1616 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (PBUH): He (PBUH) used to perform nawafl on top of his horse, no matter which direction it was facing."
"1635",": 1617 It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that he used to perform the Witr prayer on top of his horse, and he has mentioned this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (that is, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do the same)."
"1636",": 1618 Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to perform the Nafl prayer on top of his horse, and when he had to perform Witrād, he would get off the horse and perform the Witrah."
"1637",": 1619 Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps without performing Witr or forgets to perform Witr, he should perform it in the morning or when he remembers."
"1638",": 1620 Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked: If one of us prays in the morning and he has not yet performed Witrah, the Prophet (Peace be upon him) said: He should perform Witrah in the morning."
"1639",": 1621 Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Whoever commits ablution at night"","" he should make up for it the next day.\"""""""
"1640",": 1622 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Witrhaq is right and obligatory. Whoever wants to perform three Witradas should perform three, and whoever wants to perform one Rakat, then he should perform one Rakat and Witrada. Be of"
"1641",": 1623 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever wants to pray five rak'ahs"","" whoever wants to pray three rak'ahs"","" and whoever wants to pray one rak'ah.\"""""""
"1642",": 1624 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: There are twenty-five, three or one."
"1643",": 1625 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is right for whoever wants to pray seven rak'ahs in the morning, whoever wants to pray five rak'ahs, whoever wants to pray three witr's and whoever wants to pray one witr."
"1644",": 1626 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: You should perform five rak'ahs and witr's. If you cannot afford it, perform three."
"1645",": 1627 The same tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1646",": 1628 Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: It is permissible for anyone who wishes to pray five rak'ahs, whoever wishes to pray three rak'ahs, and whoever wishes to pray one rak'ah, and whoever is able to only point, let him point."
"1647","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"1648","Sayyidna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: I said, O Messenger of Allah! How much do I have? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I asked, O Prophet of Allah! I have more power than that. Then the Holy Prophet said three. Then he said five. Then he said seven. At that time, I would have accepted the leave given by the Prophet."
"1649","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the two rakats of Witr in the later rakats, and in these two rakats he would recite Surah Al-Aali and Surah Al-Kafrun, while in the second rakat he would recite Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq and Surah Al-Nas."
"1650","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: perform three rak'ahs and divide them into five or seven rak'ahs and do not compare it to Maghrib prayer."
"1651","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform three rak'ahs and alternate them with five rak'ahs or seven rak'ahs. Do not compare it to Maghrib prayer."
"1652","Qays bin Abu Hazim narrates: I saw Sayyidna Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, perform one rak'ah after Isha, so I inquired which prayer it was. So he replied, I have seen the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing one rak'ah and witrada."
"1653","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There are three Witrs of the night, just as there are three rak’ahs of the Witr of the day (i.e. the evening prayer)."
"1654","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates what the Prophet (PBUH) used to do while riding his horse."
"1655","Saeed bin Yasar Bayan says: \I got off the horse and said"","" 'Abdullah bin Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to me"","" 'Isn't the good deeds of the Messenger of Allah sufficient for you? I said yes! So he said: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do while riding?"""""
"1656","Sayyiduna Al-Khazaifah bin Hudhafa (RA) narrates that once the Prophet (PBUH) came to us, he (PBUH) said, “Allah has given you one more prayer, which is better for you than red camels.” It is the Witr prayer."
"1657","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us, and the blessed face of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, showed a state of happiness and contentment. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Allah, the Most High, has given you one more prayer, and that prayer is the Witr prayer."
